<!-- From -->
<a class=post href=http://origin.goa.com>Origin GOA France</a> has posted a new <a class=post href=http://origin.goa.com/starreng.shtml>interview with Starr Long</a> (also available <a class=post href=http://origin.goa.com/starrlong.shtml
>in French</a>); here's a bit from the interview:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
<b> 5. We already know that ORIGIN is going to have a very large game world with three continents and many different cities.<br>
 Can we know how many cities there will be?<br>
 Is it the plan to have each city have a different feel and look? </b> <br>
  <br>
  There will be eight major cities at release: Britain, Vesper, Yew, Buccaneer's Den, Ishpur, Logos, New Minoc, and Garron.<br> 
In addition there are lots of little villages scattered between these cities. Each city has a very unique style. This includes everything from the building style, building materials, colors, furniture, sky color, music, ambient sounds, and even shop signs.<br>
 There are also more striking differences; for instance, Yew is built around and in a tree that is bigger than a mountain while Logos is built on floating metal decks tethered to the ground.

  <p><b> 6.	I'd like to ask the same question about dungeons. <br>
How many will there be and will they all have different looks, feels and monsters?<br>
 Could you share with us some examples of dungeon/city design? </b><br>
    <br>
    There will be six major dungeons at release: Deceit, Despise, Covetous, Doom, The Sewers, and Hythloth. Like the cities, they will each also have different styles including building materials, lighting, ambient sounds, music, and monster populations. <br>
For instance, Doom is a living hive of Terathans (insect people) while Hythloth is a technological factory populated by its former cybernetic workers gone mad.
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


