<!-- From -->
From the <a class=post href=http://boards.uo2.com/>Official Boards</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
The entire team is pretty much going to take off for the next couple a days for the standard American holiday celebrating when the pilgrims ate turkey and watched football with the indians, so we'll probably go a little quiet here.  <br><br>However, we know we can't leave you high and dry as far as information goes, so I thought I'd share this piece of information with you all.<br><br>We currently have more than 140 individual pieces of clothing in the game right now and working.  Notes about this number:<br>+ All races can wear all items so far.<br>+ This counts only visible worn items.<br>+ This does count some jewelry, though.  For example, you can see some necklaces when they are worn.<br>+ This does not count our considerable collection of armor pieces.<br>+ Most pieces actually change the shape of your avatar, such as the coat on the Juka in the screenshot you may have seen.  Very few are merely 'painted on'.<br>+ Most items can be layered.  For example, you can wear a coat over a skirt over a thigh bracelet, and things look generally pretty good.<br>+ This number does not count variants given to us by hueing, which of course drastically increases this amount.<br>+ This only counts the stuff working -right now-.  There's still considerable more clothing to come.<br><br>I hope this gets you would-be tailors salivating.<br><br>Ubiq
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


